      "part": "problem",
      "original_record": "before",
      "value": "If $X=\\{1,3,5,7\\}$ and $Y=\\{1,2,3,4\\},$ then $Y-X=$",
      "original_html_sha256": "a54a8ff1eb94b98fd7d89f6e1a894d91c629cdd000f516b3e5cac8e4475376da",
      "extractor_sha256": "1591183da328a4140792793d2cc113fd535ab5f25bc7f284ceb1b6f251efad18",
      "source_file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/repairs/source-provenance-v2/structured-source/source/a54a8ff1eb94b98fd7d89f6e1a894d91c629cdd000f516b3e5cac8e4475376da.html",
      "extraction_errors": []
    },
    {
      "part": "worked_solution",
      "original_record": "history",
      "value": "The set $Y-X$ is the set of all elements belonging to $Y$ but *not* $X.$ Note that the elements $1,3\\in X$ are also in $Y,$ so we must remove them. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Y-X & =\\{1,2,3,4\\}-\\{1,3,5,7\\} \\\\  & =\\{2,4\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "original_html_sha256": "5eac93d9efa2138ff644878fa7d26f730a24e3f3df04b536561a640c2261cc54",
      "extractor_sha256": "1591183da328a4140792793d2cc113fd535ab5f25bc7f284ceb1b6f251efad18",
